1. GPL-3.0 -- Gisselquist Technology LLC (ZipVersa / ZipCPU project)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The networking protocol stack under fw/vebpf_network_packet_processing/lib/
is derived from the ZipVersa project by Dan Gisselquist and is licensed under
the GNU General Public License version 3 (or later). These 23 files each carry
their own GPL-3.0 header (verified file-by-file):

    lib/pkt.c        lib/pkt.h
    lib/arp.c        lib/arp.h
    lib/icmp.c       lib/icmp.h
    lib/ipproto.c    lib/ipproto.h
    lib/ipcksum.c    lib/ipcksum.h
    lib/udpproto.c   lib/udpproto.h
    lib/ethproto.c   lib/ethproto.h
    lib/bootloader.c lib/bootloader.h
    lib/txfns.c      lib/txfns.h
    lib/syscalls.c
    lib/crt0.S       lib/rvboot.S
    lib/protoconst.h lib/etcnet.h

Consult the individual file for the authoritative notice.
See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html

Three files in lib/ are NOT under GPL-3.0:
    lib/board.h   no license header; project-original board configuration
                  constants -- covered by the MIT license above
    lib/mmio.h    no license header; project-original MMIO address map
                  and helpers -- covered by the MIT license above
    lib/irq.c     released into the public domain by its author
                  (Unlicense-style notice in the file header)

Because every firmware application in apps/ links against this protocol stack,
the resulting firmware BINARIES are subject to GPL-3.0 terms. The application
sources in apps/ are themselves original work offered under the MIT license
above, but a linked binary combining them with the GPL-3.0 stack must be
distributed under GPL-3.0.

